<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Min Bin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1493–1554</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Minbin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Min Bin was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mrauk-u">Mrauk U</a> in Arakan from 1531 to 1554 and its most powerful ruler. He built up a strong navy with Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>, controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chittagong">Chittagong</a> and raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, and fortified his capital, beating off an invasion by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabinshwehti">Tabinshwehti</a> of Toungoo in 1546 to 1547. He built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shitthaung-temple">Shitthaung Temple</a>, the best-known monument of Mrauk U.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/min-bin.jpg" alt="Min Bin" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Uthantofburma at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shitthaung001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
